,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nreproducible in v4.5.beta5.official [c81fd6c51]\nnot reproducible in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta5 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7652) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 15.66 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nwhen calling an overloaded function, unrelated syntax errors later in shader code cause an erroneous error to be reported instead :\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\n\nvoid fn(int val) { }\nvoid fn(float val) { }\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tfn(1.0);\n\tfloat d = vec2(0.0);\n}\n//Error at line 7: Invalid argument for \"fn(int)\" function: argument 1 should be int but is float.\n```\ncalling the first overload defined works as expected:\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\n\nvoid fn(int val) { }\nvoid fn(float val) { }\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tfn(1);\n\tfloat d = vec2(0.0);\n}\n//Error at line 8: Invalid assignment of 'vec2' to 'float'.\n```\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6] gives the expected behaviour:\n```glsl\nshader_type canvas_item;\n\nvoid fn(int val) { }\nvoid fn(float val) { }\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tfn(1.0);\n\tfloat d = vec2(0.0);\n}\n//Error at line 8: Invalid assignment of 'vec2' to 'float'.\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\npaste the code snippets above into a shader\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"http